	)
	(text "Power tree: +5V is the TPS2116 power mux's output (U10), USB first, the console's 5 V second.\n  VBUS     USB-C (usb sheet) -> VIN1, the priority input: MODE on VIN1, PR1 from R22 33k / R23 10k, so VBUS\n           above VREF x 4.3 (3.96-4.64 V) runs the cart and the console's supply delivers nothing.\n  CONS_5V  edge pin D, the console's 5 V (spare current not published: prefer USB) -> VIN2, without USB.\n  37-60 mOhm either way; reverse current blocking: neither source back-feeds the other, so a cart on USB\n  never powers a console that is off.  ST is not used.\n+5V feeds the WS2812, U12 AP2112K -> +3V3_RP (every RP2350A supply pin: it rises with +5V, so the 5 V-tolerant\npads are never unpowered with 5 V on them) and U11 AP63203 -> +3V3 (the ESP32-S3, the CP2102N and the microSD;\nWiFi bursts ~400 mA; it waits out UVLO, then soft-starts over 4 ms).  Without USB the cart adds ~145 mA average,\n~370 mA peak to the console's supply (tools/audit/margins.py): prefer USB power.  TP9, TP8, TP10, TP11 and TP12 are\nbring-up pads."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 81.28 68.58 0)
		(effects
